premise='Fixed defaultR/B8/nooverride; all complete original WS fixture premises and independently initialized branches retained. Actual valid ordinary objects/table/type/name/party/templates/rules/UI/scene/messages/callbacks and positive-integer random domains normal to stated observation, unless a specified failure/negative return is being contrasted. Save statements distinguish requesting whole-object save from native serialization/disk/host success; no target/Ruby/native/business model execution. Tool-only empty/short/missing-template/reorder/exception inputs are not asserted ordinary UI/default Demo reachable. WS-W08 bottom-level oldRand(0) return-type premise remains explicitly OPEN; it is not silently covered by positive integer RNG or metadata.'
manual=[
 ('R09','TrainerSelect6–34','Trainer range picks the eligible row with greatest minimum wins. At N300, wins0/5 use0..99;6uses80..119;13uses120..139;14uses100..139;48uses220..259;49and50use200..299. These listed endpoints are manual constant deductions of the literal table.'),
 ('R09','TrainerSelect6–34','Wins−1 matches no row and returns integer0 before random. For N50/wins0 scaled offset0 and integer width16 give positive-domain draws0..15; no ceil scaling.'),
 ('R09','GenerateTrainer39–83','IV starts31 then descending index thresholds overwrite it; index99→3,100→6,219→21,220→31. Valid source trainer index/candidate template identities are separate premises.'),
 ('R09','GenerateTrainer39–83','Candidate count<=suggestedNumber returns every entry in source order without filling/checking the final team. Count5or40 withsuggested3 instead repeatedly samples with replacement to length3, clears on failed whole-team validation and has no iteration bound.'),
 ('R07','start79–83/DataStart205–229','Outer start sets current identity before inner start. Inner immediately writes inProgress/resting/decision/current counts/battleNumber1/trainers[] before rejecting nonpositive numRounds; old numRounds and later start/oldParty/activeparty/save writes have not happened on that rejection.'),
 ('R07','DataStart205–229','After valid positive numRounds, actual selected trainer duplicate equality is rejected by retry without a bound. If distinct values obtainable for the required fill are fewer than rounds, the loop cannot finish. Successful list completion precedes capture of start coordinates and original party.'),
 ('R07','DataStart225–229','Successful start retains oldParty by reference, replaces active party only when stored party is truthy (including empty array), and requests Game.save(safe:true) with decision already0.'),
 ('R08','Entry38–50 withR07SetParty200–203','Entry UI normal ret nil does not submit and wrapper returns nil; empty array is truthy so submits then wrapper returns Booleanfalse; nonempty submits and returns true. Direct SetParty itself stores/returns the submitted value, not this Boolean conversion.'),
 ('R07','SetParty200–203','SetParty writes active player party immediately only if inProgress, then stores the same submitted reference. Outside progress it only updates stored registration for later start.'),
 ('R07','Cancel270–273/Reset292–304','Cancel restores oldParty only if truthy then resets exactly inProgress/resting/start/decision/wins/swaps/battleNumber/trainers/oldParty/party/extraData. It preserves numRounds, outer current identity, outer rules/types/counters and requests neither save nor refresh.'),
 ('R07','OuterEnd87–93/TypeSave345–362','Outer end when identity!=−1 first saves type counters from current inner data then sets identity−1 before inner end; identity−1 bypasses type recovery. Winningdecision1 retains currentcounts; all other nonzero decisions zero currentcounts but update previous/max; decision0 zeroscurrent only and retains previous/max.'),
 ('R07','InnerEnd275–282','Inner end unconditionally assigns active player party=oldParty before checking inProgress. Inactive returns with that write and no reset/refresh/save; active snapshots decision!=0, resets, marks need_refresh and requests safe save only for that saved Boolean.'),
 ('R07','Rest258–268/SaveInProgress306–318','Active rest sets restingtrue, active continue false; neither clears inProgress. Both temporarily use start map/position/updirection, request safe save and then restore live map/position/direction on normal return, even when returned Booleanfalse.'),
 ('R07','SaveInProgress306–318','No ensure/rescue surrounds temporary map/position writes and Game.save. A propagated exception before restoration leaves the committed position prefix; it is distinct from a caught IO false return.'),
 ('WS-SAVE','save111–125','Game.save validates first, then writes safesave/save_count/magic_number/time prefix; only IOError/SystemCallError from its begin block are caught, decrementing save_count and returningfalse. Other exceptions propagate; no session rollback or disk-success guarantee follows from the request.'),
 ('R07','AddWin243–247/Match253–256','Only inProgress AddWin increments battleNumber and wins together. MatchOver is true inactive/nonzero decision or when battleNumber>numRounds, so third win frombattleNumber1 gives4>3.'),
 ('R07','InChallenge106–116/DataNext284–286','Event in-challenge delegates actual inProgress, regardless of resting. nextTrainer uses trainers[battleNumber−1]; no separate paused-state exclusion.'),
 ('R08','Graphic77–89 withTrainerType52–72','Normal charset resolver may returnnil for invalid/missing type/asset; graphic helper falls back NPC01 for falsey/empty filename, and StandardError during bitmap/dispose/name-set block also attempts NPC01. Resolver before begin or fallback setter failures are not blanket caught-success guarantees.'),
 ('R07','Register28–36','Factory registration installs extraData, forces immediate generated count3 and Tower type, while existing truthy rules reference remains retained. Reset later clears extraData; it does not clear every outer configuration.'),
 ('R07','Battle95–104 withR10Organized40–97','Single-battle wrapper result is returned to event caller without setting sessiondecision or incrementing wins/round; GamePlayer trainer-battle stats and temp dump remain local organized-wrapper responsibilities. Explicit AddWin is a separate progression input.'),
 ('R07','Data139–142','Data query first returnsnil if not inProgress; otherwise it compares currentChallenge<0 before cloning a type record. Normal active string identity raises at that comparison, so no record clone is reached.'),
 ('R09','GenerateTrainer39–83','Zero candidate numbers returns an empty opponent party after valid type/name construction with zero template creation. Missing actual numbered template instead fails at nil.createPokemon before returning an opponent; short valid1/2 returns1/2 without team validation.'),
 ('R10','Organized40–97/BattleConstructor98–174','For no-debug/noadjustment C1, player heal occurs before item snapshots and battle creation; RecordedBattle base constructor rejects empty party2. Thus empty-generated opponent can fail after player heal while old temp record/stats remain untouched by this later wrapper tail.'),
 ('R13','Adjust61–68','Without levelAdjustment, adjustLevels returnsnil and no EXP array snapshot; unadjustLevels is gated by both existing adjustment and truthy adjusts. Opponent item snapshot may independently be empty array.'),
 ('R10','Organized40–97','Debug skip precedes heal/adjust/create and returns true after three messages/clear/MEStop. Normal decided5 keepsdump but returnsfalse; ordinary postbattle cleanup and stats follow only if preceding normal sequence completes.'),
 ('R07','WS36 explicit composition ofCancel/End/Start','Given old type six counts wins5/swaps2 and roundlimit3, cancel restoresO/resetsinner while keepingoutertower/counts/limit. Following outerEnd withdecision0 zeroscurrent0/0,retainsprev/max5/2,identity−1,then inactiveinnerEndwritesnilparty withoutsave/refresh. Directdec1endinsteadrecoverscounts/restoresO/resets/refreshes/save. CancelwithoutoldPartyretainsactiveparty; cancel→restartwithoutsubmissioncapturesOandrequestsSave withoutpartyreplacement. These are manually authored finite state compositions, not executed state model.')]
